   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "7 \u00b7 SDR -> HDR (LTX-2.5 IC-LoRA). Runs AFTER the Atlas scene: the frames are either the viewport's baked camera move (toggle USE CAMERA MOVE = true; bake the move in the viewport first, re-run) or the source plate repeated 25x.\n\nNo prompt: fixed scene embeddings, cfg 1, 8 distilled steps (upstream example 3bf3ca6). Frames trimmed to 8k+1; capped to ~0.9 MP and a multiple of 32.\n\nOUTPUT: ACEScg scene-linear EXR (half) per frame in output/atlas_hdr_exr (diffuse white ~1.0, highlights above 1 are the model's reconstruction), an HLG master, and a tone-mapped preview MP4. The HDR is a model hypothesis of the highlights the SDR plate clipped, not recovered data.\n\nModels: transformer bf16 + IC-LoRA in V135 models; scene-emb copied to models/embeddings; video VAE uses the conv decoder (ltx-2.5-video-vae-bf16 is the best-quality option, not downloaded). Long or big batches can OOM in decode: shorten the move."
   ]
  }
 ],
